HST Office: HST Sheets counts dates like the leading spreadsheet application's 1900 date system (owner 18/11:
full fix in 1.0.3). In .xlsx/.xls files and new documents with its formula syntax (the HST Sheets default),
serial 1 is 01/01/1900, 59 is 28/02/1900, 60 is 29/02/1900 (the day it keeps for compatibility) and 61 is
01/03/1900; from 61 on nothing changes. Before, serial 1 was 31/12/1899 and DATE(1900,1,1) was 2 (1 in that
application). .ods files, the 1904 system, any other null date, and Writer/Impress fields are unchanged.

- svl: a switch on the document's own number formatter (SvNFLanguageData, default off, active only with the
  null date 30/12/1899): date output (cell display, TEXT) shows the 1900-system day, with the weekday of the
  serial (serial 1 is a Sunday) and 29/02/1900 for 60; input ("29/02/1900", "1/1/1900", ISO, DATEVALUE) reads
  1900-system serials. Logic in svl/source/numbers/hstexcel1900.cxx (include/svl/hstexcel1900.hxx); hooks in
  zformat.cxx (output), zforfind.cxx (input), zforlist.cxx and nfengine.hxx/numformat.hxx (the switch).
- sc: the switch follows sc::hst::Excel1900Dates (new document, after loading, during .xlsx/.xls import before
  formulas calculate); DATE/YEAR/MONTH/DAY use the 1900-system day (DATE(1900,2,29)=60, DAY(60)=29), WEEKDAY
  already matched; ISO date text in arithmetic. An .ods saved from such a document stores the days it shows
  (serial 1 is office:date-value 1900-01-01; 60 is written as 1900-02-28). Serials 0 and below keep the
  one-day shift (0 is 31/12/1899), so every typed date before 01/03/1900 reads back unchanged. Logic in
  sc/source/core/hst/hstexcel1900dates.cxx; hooks in interpr2.cxx, docsh.cxx, docsh2.cxx, xmlexprt.cxx,
  global2.cxx and the .xlsx/.xls import.
- Known limits (dates before 01/03/1900 only): DAYS360, WEEKNUM, ISOWEEKNUM, NETWORKDAYS, WORKDAY, DATEDIF,
  EDATE/EOMONTH, autofilter/pivot date grouping and non-Gregorian calendars use LibreOffice's count there.

Test: CppunitTest_svl_hst_excel1900 (day rules, output and input in en-US/vi-VN/en-GB, default off, 1904
unaffected), CppunitTest_sc_hst_excel1900_dates (display, TEXT, DATE/YEAR/MONTH/DAY/WEEKDAY/DATEVALUE, typed
dates, .xlsx round trip, an older .ods unchanged, .ods export of such a document).
